import ExportGuideLayout from '../../layouts/ExportGuideLayout.astro';
---
<ExportGuideLayout
  title="How to Export Your Students from Martialytics"
  description="Export your active student list from Martialytics as a CSV and import it into BeltManager, step by step. Sourced from Martialytics' own help pages, checked November 2026."
  heading="How to export your students from Martialytics"
  crumb="Export from Martialytics"
  locale="us"
  checked="November 6, 2026"
  ctaHeading="Ready to bring your school across?"
  sources={[
    { label: 'Martialytics Help Center: How To: Export a list of Active Students', url: 'https://intercom.help/martialytics/en/articles/4222112-how-to-export-a-list-of-active-students', note: 'Dated August 5, 2021 on the page. Read November 6, 2026.' },
    { label: 'Martialytics Help Center: How To: Navigate your Student List', url: 'https://intercom.help/martialytics/en/articles/3942178-how-to-navigate-your-student-list', note: 'Dated September 13, 2021 on the page. Read November 6, 2026.' },
  ]}
>
  <p>
    Martialytics lets you download your student list as a CSV yourself. These steps come from its help center. We haven't run them
    in a Martialytics account.
  </p>
  <h2>Export from Martialytics</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Open your <strong>Student List</strong>.</li>
    <li>Open the filters at the top of the list and choose <strong>Reset</strong>.</li>
    <li>Make sure the <strong>Active Students</strong> toggle is on, then choose <strong>Apply Filters</strong>.</li>
    <li>Choose the <strong>Export</strong> button at the bottom of the list. It's a downward arrow, and it downloads a CSV file.</li>
  </ol>
  <h2>What the file contains</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Martialytics' help pages don't list the columns in this export</strong>, so we can't tell you what's in the file. Open it before
    you import and look for the columns BeltManager needs: first name, last name and date of birth. Also look for guardian
    details, because every student under 18 needs them. If something is missing, add a column and fill it in by hand.
  </p>
  <p>
    The list can also be filtered to Inactive and Pending students. BeltManager only accepts active and trial students, so stay
    with the active list for this import.
  </p>
</ExportGuideLayout>
